y but then daniel jumped in to say  that he didn't think they lost anything  and he pointed out some of the things  that we've been talking about how they  pulled things forward to season five and  overall they sounded confident that they  pulled it off as far as what the cast  had to say they all felt like it was  surreal that they were coming to the end  of their journey bobby couldn't be there  because she was filming something else  they mentioned losing alex and how that  changes things but didn't give any more  details about how the crew would be  filled out instead each of them kind of  focused on where their character's at in  the beginning it sounds like things are  pretty rough steven strait said that  morale is really low the war is dragging  on and there's a sense that they haven't  gotten anywhere it's wearing on holden  and the rest of the crew naomi's angry  about the part that she played in alex's  death that's hanging over all of them no  one seems to be happy that clarissa is  there except for amos and they're flying  around fighting with and killing belters  and as you can imagine that's hard for  naomi west chatham brought up the fact  that amos used to use these other people  as his moral compass and now he finds  clarissa doing the same thing with him  he's starting to make his own choices  and not necessarily questioning holden  but wanting to understand things on a  deeper level it sounds like there's a  real sense of why do we have to be in  the middle of all this  nadine said that clarissa is just trying  to keep her head down and trying to  prove her worth to these people who she  tried to kill they did hint that we'll  see a lot of the aftermath of the rocks  falling on earth and they phrased it in  the way that earth gets literally  obliterated the ecosystem's breaking  down there's so many deaths and there's  so many other problems related to that  and it's all on alba serala's shoulders  she's lost her husband and there seems  to be a 